Description: Fix parent/sizer mismatch in the About dialog (panelAbout)
 Same defect as 0003, in a different dialog: panelAbout builds an inner
 wx.Panel to hold its content, but never calls panel.SetSizer() on it;
 instead the inner sizer itself is returned and set directly as the
 frame's own sizer. The label/button widgets are therefore managed by
 a sizer nested under the frame's sizer while their real parent (the
 inner panel) is never part of that hierarchy at all.
 .
 wxWidgets 3.2 (as currently shipped by Debian/Ubuntu) enforces this
 at runtime and aborts with a C++ assertion; older wxWidgets versions
 tolerated it. This crashed on opening Help > About:
 .
   wx._core.wxAssertionError: C++ assertion
   "CheckExpectedParentIs(w, m_containingWindow)" failed at
   ./src/common/sizer.cpp(887) in SetContainingWindow(): Windows
   managed by the sizer associated with the given window must have
   this window as parent, otherwise they will not be repositioned
   correctly.
 .
 Fix: give the inner panel its own sizer, and return an outer sizer
 that contains the panel itself (not the panel's own sizer).
Author: David <david@katalystnord.com>
Forwarded: https://github.com/SCIENCE-OPEN/mmassx/pull/TODO
Last-Update: 2026-09-08
--- a/gui/panel_about.py
+++ b/gui/panel_about.py
@@ -101,7 +101,12 @@ class panelAbout(frame):
         sizer.Add(cite_butt, 0, wx.CENTER|wx.LEFT|wx.RIGHT|wx.BOTTOM, 20)
         
         sizer.Fit(panel)
-        return sizer
+        panel.SetSizer(sizer)
+
+        outerSizer = wx.BoxSizer(wx.VERTICAL)
+        outerSizer.Add(panel, 1, wx.EXPAND)
+
+        return outerSizer
     # ----
     
     
